PRIVATE REFLECTION: The Black centre consists of three components with the liberties listed in round 3:

G1=A2 : {A1,A3,B2}
G2=B3–B4 : {A3,A4,B2}
G3=C1–C2 : {B1,B2}
Only empty points A1,A3,A4,B1,B2 can touch a Black liberty. White’s right side D1–D2–C3–C4–D5 is alive with multiple outside liberties, no forced defensive first move is required.

Analysis of the five candidate first moves:

1.W B1 puts G3 in atari on B2. Black is forced to 2.B B2 else 2.W B2 captures G3. After 2.B B2 A2–B2–B3–B4–C1–C2 merges to {A1,A3,A4} and W B1 is left with single liberty A1, 3.B A1 captures B1. 1…B A1 loses G3 to 2.W B2. B1 is a sacrificial self-atari, not a net.

1.W B2 puts G3 in atari on B1 and W B2 itself is in atari on B1. The only saving defence is 2.B B1. 2.B B1 is legal: the newly placed B1 has liberties A1 and the now-empty B2 before capture resolution, so it is not self-atari. 2.B B1 captures W B2 and joins B1 to G3. After capture:
B1–C1–C2 : {A1,B2}
A2 : {A1,A3,B2}
B3–B4 : {A3,A4,B2}
3.W A1 is illegal suicide – A1 adjacent to A2 and B1 with no capture. 3.W B2 is snap-back 4.B C2 recaptures. 3.W A3 is met by 4.B A4 capturing A3 or 4.B B2 reconnecting centre. No forced net emerges.

1.W A1 is captured at once by 2.B B1.
1.W A3 is self-atari on A4; met by 2.B A4 capturing A3 or 2.B B2 connecting A2–B3–B4–C1–C2 to A1,A3,A4.
1.W A4 is met by 2.B B2 which connects A2–B3–B4–C1–C2 to A1,A3,B1 and leaves W A4 in atari.

Earlier claims for {A3} and {B2} as forcing nets are refuted by the legal 2.B B1 defence after 1.W B2 and the suicide/illegal-net arguments above. Colleagues 4 and 6 in round 0 who argued {A3} and {B2} have been corrected in rounds 1-3.

Current consensus after round 3: Colleagues 1,2,3,4,5,6,7 all output {}. No first move puts a Black group into unavoidable atari against all Black replies. My current belief remains the set of guaranteed-kill first moves is empty: {}.

Unresolved: none. The key persistent facts are the liberty sets, legality of 2.B B1 after 1.W B2, illegality of 3.W A1 suicide, and that White right side needs no defence.

